          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Political Rise</strong><br>\nIndira Gandhi was born into a politically influential family as the daughter of Jawaharlal Nehru, India's first Prime Minister.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ascension as Prime Minister</strong><br>\nShe served as Prime Minister from 1966 to 1977 and then from 1980 until her assassination in 1984, being the first and, to date, the only female Prime Minister of India.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Major Reforms and Policies</strong><br>\nGandhi implemented major reforms in agriculture that resulted in India's self-sufficiency in food grain production and led to her being known as the architect of the Green Revolution in India.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Emergency Period</strong><br>\nHer decision to declare a state of emergency in 1975 suspended citizens' rights, led to widespread arrests, and is one of the most controversial periods of her leadership.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Foreign Policy Initiatives</strong><br>\nHer tenure saw significant foreign policy alignments, including the Indo-Soviet treaty and India's involvement in the liberation of Bangladesh in 1971.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Operation Blue Star</strong><br>\nIn 1984, she ordered Operation Blue Star to remove Sikh extremists from the Golden Temple, which led to her assassination by her own Sikh bodyguards.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
